/E (The analysis identifies a significant infrastructure gap of 75 new stations required across 47 counties. We recommend that the Ministry of Transport and private investors prioritize deployment in counties with the highest predicted need, such as Nairobi \(5 new stations\), Mombasa \(6\), Kiambu \(8\), and Nakuru \(4\), to address the most severe service deficiencies first.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (The KMeans clustering model provides optimized, data-driven co-ordinates for new stations within each county. We recommend that investors and utility providers use these generated co-ordinates as primary candidates for site feasibility studies, rather than relying on arbitrary or centralized placement, to ensure broader population coverage and reduce clustering.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
